    "result_text": "The change is complete and the test passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change lets you narrow a project's task checklist to **just the open** or **just the finished** tasks. It was a front-end-only change \u2014 the `tasks` table, its `done` flag, and the `/api/projects/{projectId}/tasks` endpoint already existed, so no migration or server work was needed.\n\nFollowing the app's additive conventions (mirroring the existing invoices status-filter), the change is mostly **new files**:\n\n- **`slots/defs/projectTasksToolbar.ts`** (new) \u2014 declares a toolbar region above the tasks checklist.\n- **`features/tasks/filter.slot.tsx`** (new) \u2014 the `task-filter` `<select>` (All / OPEN / DONE) that owns the `taskFilter` URL search param (rule 4) and fills the toolbar region (rule 3).\n- **`features/tasks/queries.ts`** \u2014 added the shared `TASK_FILTER_PARAM` key and `TASK_FILTERS` values.\n- **`features/tasks/ProjectTasksTable.tsx`** \u2014 renders the toolbar slot and reads the same `taskFilter` key to drop rows at the other status. The control and the table stay in step through the URL key alone \u2014 no callback, no shared state.\n\nState lives in the URL, the control is self-contained, and nothing imports across features \u2014 consistent with CLAUDE.md. `npm run typecheck` passes and `bin/e2e` shows the acceptance spec green (3 \u2192 2 open \u2192 1 done).",
